/T (Central tendency: The mean and median of Placement_Percentage\(63.13% and 63.30% respectively\) are close to one another, suggesting a broadly symmetric central distribution for this indicator. Average_Salary_LPA shows a larger gap between mean \(5.78\) and median \(5.41\), which, together with a maximum value of 30.96 far above the third quartile of 6.67, indicates a right-skewed distribution with a small number of comparatively high-salary records pulling the mean upward relative to the median. )
/E (Central tendency: The mean and median of Placement_Percentage\(63.13% and 63.30% respectively\) are close to one another, suggesting a broadly symmetric central distribution for this indicator. Average_Salary_LPA shows a larger gap between mean \(5.78\) and median \(5.41\), which, together with a maximum value of 30.96 far above the third quartile of 6.67, indicates a right-skewed distribution with a small number of comparatively high-salary records pulling the mean upward relative to the median. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [39]
>>
