747 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 332 0 R
/E (The data shows that Tier 1 institutions exhibit the strongest average performance across all four quantitative indicators placement \(72.93%\), salary \(9.99 LPA\), internship participation \(65.89%\) and employability \(73.26\). Tier 2 institutions also perform strongly, particularly on employability \(72.00\) and placement \(69.95%\), positioning Tier 2 closer to Tier 1 than to Tier 3 or Tier4 on these two measures. Tier 3 and Tier 4 show relatively similar average quantitative performance across all four indicators, with differences between them generally under one percentage point. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [54]
>>
endobj
748 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 332 0 R
/E (This pattern is presented strictly as an observed association: Tier 1 classification is not claimed to cause stronger placement outcomes. The association may reflect a combination of institutional characteristics, industry exposure, recruiter demand, student profile and other factors that were not isolated in this analysis. It should also be noted that the record distribution across tiers is highly uneven. Tier 4 alone accounts for 62.95% of all records and this imbalance should be kept in mind when interpreting tier- level comparisons. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [55]
>>
endobj
