/T (Interpretation: The college comparison analysis reveals substantial variation in placement performance across both engineering branches and institutional tiers. CSE, IT and Emerging Technology domains demonstrate comparatively stronger placement outcomes across tiers, whereas Civil and Mechanical Engineering show lower performance, particularly in Tier 3 and Tier 4 institutions. The results suggest that recruiter shortlisting can be made more effective by considering branch-specific performance alongside institutional tier rather than using college tier as the sole selection criterion.)
/E (Interpretation: The college comparison analysis reveals substantial variation in placement performance across both engineering branches and institutional tiers. CSE, IT and Emerging Technology domains demonstrate comparatively stronger placement outcomes across tiers, whereas Civil and Mechanical Engineering show lower performance, particularly in Tier 3 and Tier 4 institutions. The results suggest that recruiter shortlisting can be made more effective by considering branch-specific performance alongside institutional tier rather than using college tier as the sole selection criterion.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [5]
