/Title (Descriptive statistics show an overall mean placement percentage of approximately 63.13%, mean average salary of approximately 5.78 LPA, mean internship participation of approximately 54.69%, and mean employability indicator of approximately 61.72%. Branch-level analysis indicates that Computer Science Engineering records the highest average placement \(74.36%\) and salary \(7.16 LPA\), while Civil Engineering records the lowest average placement \(49.34%\) and salary \(4.28 LPA\). Tier-level analysis indicates that Tier 1 institutions show the strongest average performance across all four quantitative indicators, while Tier 3 and Tier 4 show relatively similar average performance.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 52 0 R
/Prev 2605 0 R
/Next 2916 0 R
>>
endobj
2916 0 obj
<<
/Title (A project-defined Recruiter Readiness framework was developed using Placement Percentage, Employability Indicator and Internship Participation to classify institutions as Recruiter Ready, Moderately Ready or Needs Improvement. This framework, together with descriptive fields on curriculum subjects, recruiter demand, industry skills, and skill gaps, was translated into a set of Power BI dashboards supporting recruiter-oriented college and branch shortlisting.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 52 0 R
/Prev 2915 0 R
/Next 2606 0 R
>>
endobj
